<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Amphrȳsus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ŏs</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμφρυσός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small river in the Thessalian
				province of Phthiotis</i>, <i>near which Apollo
				fed the flocks of Admetus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 1,
				580</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 229</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 3,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Am-phrȳsĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>belonging to Amphrysus</i>,
			or, <b>poet.</b> transf., <i>to
			Apollo</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vates,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the Sibyl</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 398</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Am-phrȳsĭăcus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gramen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 1, 4, 105</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
